  "id": "linux-nvidia-dgx-spark-2x-qwen38-flash-next-sglang",
  "name": "2x DGX Spark Qwen3.8 Flash Next NVFP4 SGLang",
  "version": 19,
  "summary": "On-demand two-Spark SGLang TP=2 Qwen3.8 Flash Next with a measured two-request entity-workload envelope, LLooM-owned overflow queueing, scheduler-safe disconnect cancellation, stable target-only decode, native low-effort reasoning, SM121 QSA guards, NVFP4 KV, native 262K context, and reserved sidecar headroom.",
  "license": { "id": "MIT", "name": "Recipe metadata and launcher" },
  "provenance": {
    "createdBy": "lloom",
    "generatedBy": "manual-curated",
    "source": "Adapted from MiaAI-Lab/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-Dual-DGX-Sparks 0f950012c8d8323acac9a08846a32ef7953f5f62 with LLooM-native distributed lifecycle, FP32 recurrent state, a measured-sidecar target, a two-request scheduler profile, an exact-source-guarded SGLang PR #36418 disconnect lifecycle fix, atomic token-id-0 cache reclamation, and target-only production decode after a single-request speculative-verify failure"
  },
  "links": [
    { "rel": "upstream", "href": "https://github.com/MiaAI-Lab/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-Dual-DGX-Sparks/tree/0f950012c8d8323acac9a08846a32ef7953f5f62" },
    { "rel": "comparison", "href": "https://github.com/tonyd2wild/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVFP4-DGX-Spark" },
    { "rel": "model", "href": "https://huggingface.co/RadixArk/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVFP4/tree/7b719225242aacd3dbd3f9407468c2ee9a9d2594" },
    { "rel": "runtime", "href": "https://hub.docker.com/r/lmsysorg/sglang/tags" }
  ],
  "keywords": ["linux", "nvidia", "dgx-spark", "cluster", "qwen3.8", "flash-next", "nvfp4", "sglang", "qsa", "sidecars"],
  "capabilities": ["chat", "responses", "anthropic-messages", "streaming", "usage", "tools", "reasoning", "vision", "moe", "long-context"],
  "hardware": {
    "family": "NVIDIA DGX Spark / GB10",
    "testedMachine": "Two directly connected DGX Spark systems",
    "notes": [
      "TP=2 runs over the private ConnectX-7 RoCE fabric and starts worker-first under LLooM. NCCL selects the IPv4 RoCE-v2 GID independently on each Spark because the kernel may assign different GID-table indexes to the same fabric address class.",
      "The SM121 packed-varlen QSA kernel, NVFP4-KV layer, and token-id-0 abort/reset guard are pinned to MiaAI-Lab commit 0f950012c8d8323acac9a08846a32ef7953f5f62; all source edits refuse mismatched anchors.",
      "The pinned SGLang revision drops tokenizer state before its delayed disconnect abort, leaving scheduler-owned zombie requests. An exact-source-guarded backport of sglang#36418 retains dispatched request IDs and forces their scheduler abort after the existing two-second teardown window.",
      "The 627648-token pool supports two simultaneous native-context working sets. LLooM admits two entity requests and owns a bounded eight-request overflow queue so later long prefills do not enter SGLang while active decodes are still making progress.",
      "Target-only production decode needs at most two active recurrent paths. The 16-path FP32 cache retains diagnostic headroom without returning to the old eight-request admission profile.",
      "Historical speculative-decode measurements with recovered Presence traffic produced three staggered requests at roughly 148K aggregate tokens. Three-way decode reached roughly 86-90 aggregate token/s, but an arriving long prefill cut generation to roughly 44 token/s; a saturated 92-second cap-three window averaged 57.9-second TTFT and 120.9-second end-to-end latency. Cap two kept overflow in LLooM and its measured 92-second window averaged 8.0-second TTFT and 46.8-second end-to-end latency.",
      "A live twelve-way staggered canary produced non-finite speculative-verify logits and token-id-0 loops in four tail streams, and a later single-request canary reproduced the same failure after 18 output tokens. Production therefore uses target-only decode; the token-id-0 guard atomically clears all cache allocators if the safety condition is ever reached again.",
      "The 0.80 static-memory fraction covers FP32 recurrent state and the NVFP4 token pool while retaining headroom for controlled experiments; 0.76 was insufficient in the former speculative profile.",
      "Generic NEXTN renders as EAGLE in this runtime, does not enforce custom thinking-budget processors, and is disabled by default because its verify path produced non-finite logits on the pinned artifact.",
      "The new SM121 kernel passed upstream exact retrieval at 120K, 190K, and 210K with no token-id-0 output; this LLooM NVFP4-KV combination still requires its own long-context semantic soak before 262K is trusted."
    ]
  },
